    <fullName>Button_Label__c</fullName>
    <defaultValue>&apos;Continue&apos;</defaultValue>
    <description>The text of this page's main forward button. In page-by-page forms it is the Next or Continue button; on the last visible page the template's Submit Button Label (or Review Page Button Label when the review screen is on) wins when set, and this value is the fallback. In Stages Mode it labels the start button on this page's stage card, showing Start Step when blank. Picklist values, so Translation Workbench translates them. Defaults to Continue; the first page of a new Stages Mode template starts as Start Step.</description>
    <inlineHelpText>Choose the text for this page's main forward button: the Next/Continue button in the linear runtime, or the start-step button on the stage card in Stages Mode. Pick something action-oriented (Continue, Apply Now, Submit Application); the picklist values translate through Translation Workbench so respondents see them in their own language.</inlineHelpText>
